1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,294
I CAN'T BELIEVE

2
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:03,754
MY LITTLE BROTHER
IS MARRIED.

3
00:00:03,796 --> 00:00:05,088
I KNOW.

4
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,340
( squeals )

5
00:00:06,381 --> 00:00:08,216
YOU GUYS, WHY
DIDN'T YOU TELL ME

6
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:09,384
YOU WERE ELOPING?

7
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:10,970
WE WERE AT THE COURTHOUSE.

8
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,387
WE WERE HAVING LUNCH...

9
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:14,890
WAIT. WHY WERE YOU
AT THE COURTHOUSE?

10
00:00:14,932 --> 00:00:16,767
WE WERE HAVING LUNCH.

11
00:00:17,852 --> 00:00:19,394
YEAH, AND THEN
ALL OF A SUDDEN, WE WERE, LIKE

12
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:20,479
"HEY, YOU KNOW, WE'RE HERE.

13
00:00:20,521 --> 00:00:21,271
WE'RE HAVING LUNCH.

14
00:00:21,313 --> 00:00:23,106
LET'S GET MARRIED!" RIGHT?

15
00:00:23,315 --> 00:00:24,483
WOW. A YEAR
AND A HALF AGO

16
00:00:24,525 --> 00:00:25,860
I DIDN'T EVEN KNOW
I HAD A BROTHER.

17
00:00:25,901 --> 00:00:27,945
NOW I HAVE
A SISTER, TOO.

18
00:00:27,987 --> 00:00:31,281
( all laughing )

19
00:00:31,323 --> 00:00:32,658
OH, IT'S SO
GREAT. OH...

20
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:36,036
( moaning )

21
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:38,246
OKAY.

22
00:00:38,288 --> 00:00:40,165
OKAY.

23
00:00:40,207 --> 00:00:41,709
STOP IT. DON'T.

24
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,418
OH.

25
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,170
SO, OOH, I'M GOING
TO GET YOU A GIFT NOW.

26
00:00:45,212 --> 00:00:47,255
IS THERE
ANYTHING YOU NEED?

27
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:50,843
OH... YEAH.

28
00:00:50,885 --> 00:00:52,845
WE'VE BEEN TRYING
TO GET PREGNANT

29
00:00:52,887 --> 00:00:54,137
UH, PRETTY MUCH EVER SINCE

30
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:55,096
WE GOT ENGAGED.

31
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:56,849
THOUGHT WE'D GET
A JUMP ON THINGS.

32
00:00:56,891 --> 00:00:58,517
YOU KNOW, NO ONE'S
GETTING ANY YOUNGER.

33
00:00:58,559 --> 00:00:59,852
( laughing )

34
00:00:59,894 --> 00:01:01,020
'CAUSE THE THING IS

35
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,855
UM, WE'RE NOT ABLE TO,
YOU KNOW

36
00:01:02,897 --> 00:01:05,024
UH, CONCEIVE,
YOU KNOW?

37
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:06,107
AND WE'VE TRIED EVERYTHING.

38
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:07,609
WE'VE SEEN
A BUNCH OF DOCTORS.

39
00:01:07,651 --> 00:01:08,861
YEAH, AND THEY...
THEY SAY THAT...

40
00:01:08,903 --> 00:01:10,905
THAT OUR ONLY CHANCE
TO HAVE A BABY

41
00:01:10,946 --> 00:01:12,907
IS IF THEY TAKE MY SPERM

42
00:01:12,948 --> 00:01:16,201
HER EGG, AND PUT IT
TOGETHER IN A DISH

43
00:01:16,243 --> 00:01:18,620
AND THEN PUT IT
INTO ANOTHER GIRL.

44
00:01:18,662 --> 00:01:19,914
SO WE WERE WONDERING

45
00:01:19,955 --> 00:01:22,416
IF YOU COULD BE THE GIRL
THAT WE COULD PUT IT INTO.

46
00:01:26,754 --> 00:01:28,589
THAT'S A REALLY
NICE GIFT.

47
00:01:30,674 --> 00:01:32,676
I WAS THINKING OF,
LIKE, A GRAVY BOAT.

48
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:44,145
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

49
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:46,648
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

50
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:49,026
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

51
00:01:49,068 --> 00:01:52,905
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS STUCK
IN SECOND GEAR ♪

52
00:01:52,947 --> 00:01:55,574
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

53
00:01:55,616 --> 00:01:59,244
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

54
00:01:59,286 --> 00:02:01,956
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

55
00:02:01,997 --> 00:02:04,207
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

56
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:06,919
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

57
00:02:06,961 --> 00:02:09,337
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

58
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:12,633
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

59
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:14,885
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

60
00:02:22,601 --> 00:02:23,894
HEY! YOU GUYS.

61
00:02:23,936 --> 00:02:25,437
CHECK IT OUT,
CHECK IT OUT.

62
00:02:25,479 --> 00:02:27,064
GUESS WHAT JOB
I JUST GOT.

63
00:02:29,357 --> 00:02:34,488
I DON'T KNOW, BUT DONALD TRUMP
WANTS HIS BLUE BLAZER BLACK.

64
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:35,906
WHAT?

65
00:02:35,948 --> 00:02:37,574
BLUE BLAZER BACK.

66
00:02:37,616 --> 00:02:40,744
HE-HE WANTS IT BACK.

67
00:02:40,786 --> 00:02:42,203
WELL, Y-YOU SAID "BLACK."

68
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:44,706
WHY WOULD HE WANT
HIS BLUE BLAZER BLACK?

69
00:02:44,748 --> 00:02:48,251
WELL, YOU-YOU KNOW WHAT I MEANT.

70
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:49,878
NO. YOU'VE MESSED IT UP.

71
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:53,340
YOU'RE STUPID.

72
00:02:55,509 --> 00:02:57,970
SO, WHAT JOB DID YOU GET, JOE?

73
00:02:58,012 --> 00:02:59,805
OH. UH, TOUR GUIDE
AT THE MUSEUM.

74
00:02:59,847 --> 00:03:01,389
YEAH. ROSS
GOT IT FOR ME.

75
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:04,101
DON'T YOU HAVE TO BE
A DINOSAUR EXPERT OR SOMETHING?

76
00:03:04,143 --> 00:03:05,310
NO, NOT REALLY.

77
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:07,186
THEY GIVE YOU ALL
THE INFORMATION.

78
00:03:07,228 --> 00:03:09,857
IT'S, UH, IT'S LIKE
MEMORIZING A SCRIPT. YEAH.

79
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:12,442
"AND ON YOUR LEFT,
YOU HAVE TYRANNOSAURUS REX

80
00:03:12,484 --> 00:03:14,528
A CARNIVORE
FROM THE JURASSIC PERIOD."

81
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:16,488
( appreciative remarks )

82
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:17,656
UH, ACTUALLY, JOEY

83
00:03:17,698 --> 00:03:20,534
IT'S THE
CRETACEOUS PERIOD.

84
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:24,955
YEAH, BUT I CAN
PRONOUNCE "JURASSIC."

85
00:03:24,997 --> 00:03:26,205
All:
HEY.
HEY!

86
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:27,374
GUESS WHAT?

87
00:03:27,415 --> 00:03:29,250
FRANK, JR. AND ALICE
GOT MARRIED.

88
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:31,336
( excited comments )

89
00:03:31,378 --> 00:03:32,963
AND THEY'RE HAVING A BABY.

90
00:03:33,005 --> 00:03:34,756
( all gasping )

91
00:03:34,798 --> 00:03:38,135
AND, AND, THEY WANT ME TO
GROW IT FOR THEM IN MY UTERUS.

92
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,681
OH, MY GOD.

93
00:03:42,723 --> 00:03:43,932
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

94
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:45,059
YEAH.

95
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:46,935
YOU'RE REALLY THINKING

96
00:03:46,977 --> 00:03:49,771
OF HAVING SEX
WITH YOUR BROTHER?

97
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:53,901
EWW! AND, OH NO!

98
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:56,403
IT'S... THEY WANT ME
TO BE THE SURROGATE.

99
00:03:56,444 --> 00:03:59,740
IT'S HER EGG AND HIS SPERM,
AND I'M-I'M JUST THE OVEN.

100
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:01,241
IT'S TOTALLY THEIR BUN.

101
00:04:01,282 --> 00:04:02,367
OH.

102
00:04:02,409 --> 00:04:03,702
WHAT DID YOU TELL THEM?

103
00:04:03,744 --> 00:04:04,786
WELL, THEY SAID

104
00:04:04,828 --> 00:04:06,371
I HAD TO THINK ABOUT IT FIRST

105
00:04:06,413 --> 00:04:07,998
BUT WHAT IS THERE TO THINK OF?

106
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,875
I'M GOING TO BE GIVING SOMEONE

107
00:04:09,917 --> 00:04:11,919
THE GREATEST GIFT
YOU CAN POSSIBLY GIVE.

108
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,754
YOU'RE GOING TO CARRY
THEIR CHILD AND GET THEM

109
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:15,630
A SONY PLAY STATION?

110
00:04:17,883 --> 00:04:21,302
HONEY, THIS REALLY IS AN
INCREDIBLE THING TO DO FOR THEM

111
00:04:21,344 --> 00:04:23,597
BUT THERE ARE THINGS
TO THINK ABOUT.

112
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:25,974
YEAH. I MEAN,
YOU'D BE PREGNANT.

113
00:04:26,016 --> 00:04:27,434
I MEAN, PREGNANT.

114
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:30,187
I KNOW.

115
00:04:30,229 --> 00:04:31,396
PHEEBS, YOU'RE TALKING

116
00:04:31,438 --> 00:04:33,148
ABOUT PUTTING YOUR BODY
THROUGH AN AWFUL LOT.

117
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:37,027
I MEAN, MORNING SICKNESS,
UH... LABOR

118
00:04:37,069 --> 00:04:38,862
AND IT'S ALL
FOR SOMEBODY ELSE.

119
00:04:38,904 --> 00:04:41,322
YEAH. WHAT'S YOUR POINT?

120
00:04:41,364 --> 00:04:45,202
WELL, THE STUFF
I JUST MENTIONED.

121
00:04:45,244 --> 00:04:47,287
WOW. I DON'T KNOW
IF I COULD EVER DO THAT.

122
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:49,831
YOU KNOW, I ALWAYS FIGURED
THE FIRST TIME I HAD A BABY

123
00:04:49,873 --> 00:04:53,919
IT WOULD BE WITH SOMEONE I LOVE,
AND THAT BABY WAS, YOU KNOW...

124
00:04:53,961 --> 00:04:56,130
A KEEPER.

125
00:04:56,171 --> 00:04:58,006
YOU KNOW, YOU GUYS WERE
A LOT MORE SUPPORTIVE

126
00:04:58,048 --> 00:05:00,968
WHEN I WANTED
TO MAKE DENIM FURNITURE.

127
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:02,970
PHEEBS, LISTEN,
IF YOU DECIDE TO DO THIS

128
00:05:03,011 --> 00:05:04,596
WE'LL BE SUPPORTIVE
LIKE CRAZY.

129
00:05:04,638 --> 00:05:05,388
YEAH.
YEAH.

130
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:06,389
JUST THINK
IT THROUGH.

131
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:08,433
TALK TO SOMEBODY
WHO'S HAD A BABY.

132
00:05:08,475 --> 00:05:09,768
LIKE YOUR MOM.

133
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:11,436
MY MOM NEVER GAVE BIRTH.

134
00:05:11,478 --> 00:05:14,856
OH, BUT MY BIRTH MOM DID.

135
00:05:20,028 --> 00:05:23,157
MMM, I LOVE THIS TUSHIE.

136
00:05:23,198 --> 00:05:24,866
CAN I TAKE IT
TO WORK WITH ME?

137
00:05:24,908 --> 00:05:26,952
OH, YEAH, SURE.
IT'S NOT MINE ANYWAY.

138
00:05:26,994 --> 00:05:28,369
IT CAME WITH THE PANTS.

139
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:29,579
OH.

140
00:05:34,209 --> 00:05:36,253
I AM SO JEALOUS.

141
00:05:36,295 --> 00:05:38,964
YOU GUYS ARE REALLY
JUST RIGHT THERE, AREN'T YOU?

142
00:05:39,006 --> 00:05:40,966
YES.

143
00:05:41,008 --> 00:05:42,801
RIGHT WHERE?

144
00:05:42,843 --> 00:05:46,930
THE BEGINNING WHERE...
YOU KNOW, IT'S ALL SEX

145
00:05:46,972 --> 00:05:50,684
AND TALKING AND SEX
AND TALKING AND...

146
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:53,061
YEAH. YOU-YOU GOT TO LOVE
THE TALKING.

147
00:05:54,104 --> 00:05:55,563
AND THE SEX?

148
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:57,149
WE HAVEN'T HAD SEX YET.

149
00:05:57,191 --> 00:05:58,900
OKAY, BUT WHAT'S

150
00:05:58,942 --> 00:06:00,319
THE BIG DEAL, YOU KNOW?

151
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:02,654
THIS IS SPECIAL,
AND I WANT OUR LOVE TO GROW

152
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:04,656
BEFORE WE MOVE
ON TO THE NEXT LEVEL.

153
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:07,326
OH, CHANDLER,
THAT IS SO NICE.

154
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:08,994
THAT IS REALLY NICE...

155
00:06:09,036 --> 00:06:11,038
LYING.

156
00:06:12,247 --> 00:06:13,874
NO WAY IS THAT
THE REASON.

157
00:06:13,915 --> 00:06:15,374
WHY?

158
00:06:15,416 --> 00:06:18,419
JUST BECAUSE YOU'RE
NOT MATURE ENOUGH TO UNDERSTAND?

159
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:19,546
NO, HE'S RIGHT.

160
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:20,755
I'M TOTALLY LYING.

161
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,054
THEN WHAT IS IT?

162
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:29,388
WELL, KATHY'S LAST BOYFRIEND
WAS JOEY.

163
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:32,559
AND YOU'RE AFRAID
YOU WON'T BE ABLE TO...

164
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:35,312
"FILL HIS SHOES."

165
00:06:35,354 --> 00:06:39,316
NO, I'M AFRAID I WON'T BE ABLE
TO MAKE LOVE AS WELL AS HIM.

166
00:06:39,358 --> 00:06:42,819
YEAH. I WAS GOING
FOR THE METAPHOR.

167
00:06:42,861 --> 00:06:46,740
YES, AND I WAS SAYING
THE ACTUAL WORDS.

168
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:47,741
Monica:
WELL, BIG DEAL.

169
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:48,867
SO JOEY'S HAD A
LOT OF GIRLFRIENDS.

170
00:06:48,909 --> 00:06:50,827
THAT DOESN'T MEAN
HE'S GREAT IN BED.

171
00:06:50,869 --> 00:06:54,873
WE SHARE A WALL.

172
00:06:54,915 --> 00:06:56,208
SO EITHER HE'S GREAT IN BED

173
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:59,794
OR SHE JUST LIKED
TO AGREE WITH HIM A LOT.

174
00:06:59,836 --> 00:07:01,755
SWEETIE, WITH YOU, IT'S
GOING TO BE DIFFERENT.

175
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:02,756
THE SEX IS GOING
TO BE GREAT

176
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:06,051
'CAUSE YOU-YOU
GUYS ARE IN LOVE.

177
00:07:06,093 --> 00:07:06,634
YEAH?

178
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:07,426
Rachel:
YEAH.

179
00:07:07,468 --> 00:07:08,427
JUST GO FOR IT, CHANDLER.

180
00:07:08,469 --> 00:07:09,971
YEAH. YOU SHOULD.
YEAH.

181
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:14,142
ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT.
I'LL SLEEP WITH MY GIRLFRIEND

182
00:07:14,184 --> 00:07:17,020
BUT I'M JUST DOING IT
FOR YOU GUYS.

183
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:25,528
OKAY. NOW THE MASTODON IS FROM
THE SEMI-LATE JURASSIC PERIOD.

184
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:28,489
ISN'T THE MASTODON
FROM THE PLIOCENE EPOCH?

185
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:30,742
SHH. THIS IS A MUSEUM.

186
00:07:30,784 --> 00:07:32,535
NO TALKING.

187
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:36,373
OKAY. RIGHT DOWN HERE,
WE HAVE...

188
00:07:36,415 --> 00:07:40,168
A LARGE FOOT.

189
00:07:40,210 --> 00:07:44,256
UH... AND OVER HERE,
WE HAVE ROSS GELLER.

190
00:07:44,298 --> 00:07:46,174
EVERYONE WAVE
HI TO ROSS.

191
00:07:46,216 --> 00:07:49,219
ROSS IS ONE OF OUR MOST
IMPORTANT SCIENTISTS.

192
00:07:49,261 --> 00:07:50,678
LOOK AT HIM
HARD AT WORK.

193
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:57,727
OKAY. MOVING
RIGHT ALONG.

194
00:07:57,769 --> 00:07:59,396
COME ON.

195
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:02,816
( knocking on door )

196
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:04,192
IT'S OPEN.
COME IN.

197
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:05,526
HI.
HI.

198
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:06,736
I'M SORRY I'M LATE.

199
00:08:06,778 --> 00:08:08,196
OH, THAT'S OKAY.

200
00:08:08,238 --> 00:08:10,865
IT GAVE ME TIME TO FINISH,
UH, GLAZING MY NIPPLES.

201
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:15,162
WOW. YOU REALLY GO ALL OUT
WHEN YOU'RE EXPECTING COMPANY.

202
00:08:15,203 --> 00:08:17,705
NO, I WAS WORKING ON MY POTTERY.

203
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:22,043
OH. OH! OH, I DIDN'T KNOW
THAT YOU DID...

204
00:08:22,085 --> 00:08:24,045
POT.

205
00:08:24,087 --> 00:08:26,423
WELL, YEAH, UH,
MOSTLY NUDES.

206
00:08:26,465 --> 00:08:30,427
IT COMBINES
MY TWO PASSIONS:
POTTERY AND EROTICA.

207
00:08:30,469 --> 00:08:32,429
OH. OOH! "ERROTERY."

208
00:08:32,471 --> 00:08:33,638
HEY! OKAY.

209
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:35,807
WELL, THANKS FOR
COMING OUT TO SEE ME.

210
00:08:35,849 --> 00:08:38,185
I JUST THOUGHT IT WOULD
BE A VERY GOOD IDEA

211
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:40,437
TO TALK ABOUT THIS
BABY STUFF IN PERSON.

212
00:08:40,479 --> 00:08:42,147
OKAY.

213
00:08:42,189 --> 00:08:43,398
( sighs )

214
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:45,484
I DON'T THINK IT'S
A VERY GOOD IDEA.

215
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:48,528
WHY NOT?

216
00:08:48,569 --> 00:08:50,697
WELL, BECAUSE YOU'D
BE GIVING UP A BABY

217
00:08:50,738 --> 00:08:52,615
AND I-I REALLY DON'T...

218
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:55,452
I DON'T KNOW IF
THERE'S ANYTHING
THAT I COULD SAY

219
00:08:55,494 --> 00:08:57,787
THAT COULD MAKE YOU
UNDERSTAND THE PAIN

220
00:08:57,829 --> 00:08:59,747
OF GIVING UP
A BABY, SO...

221
00:08:59,789 --> 00:09:01,249
UM...

222
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:02,917
( gasps )

223
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:05,253
OH, NO, NO, NO.
I UNDERSTAND THE PAIN.

224
00:09:05,295 --> 00:09:07,839
DON'T-DON'T HURT THE PUPPY.

225
00:09:07,881 --> 00:09:10,342
NO, NO, NO.
THE PUPPY IS YOURS.

226
00:09:10,384 --> 00:09:11,676
OH, I GET A PUPPY?

227
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:12,886
WELL, YEAH.

228
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:14,721
I MEAN, BUT FOR
ONLY THREE DAYS.

229
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:17,349
WHY?

230
00:09:17,391 --> 00:09:18,558
WELL, YOU KNOW

231
00:09:18,599 --> 00:09:20,601
I-I REALIZE THAT I
DON'T HAVE ANY RIGHT

232
00:09:20,643 --> 00:09:23,522
TO START GETTING
ALL PARENTY ON YOU
AND EVERYTHING NOW

233
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:25,440
BUT, UM... UH...

234
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:30,611
PHOEBE, WOULD YOU
PLEASE LOOK AT ME

235
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:31,821
AND NOT THE PUPPY?

236
00:09:31,863 --> 00:09:33,281
IT'S VERY IMPORTANT.

237
00:09:33,323 --> 00:09:34,491
OKAY.

238
00:09:34,533 --> 00:09:36,451
I MEAN, I KNOW WHAT
I'M TALKING ABOUT.

239
00:09:36,493 --> 00:09:37,869
I GAVE UP TWO BABIES

240
00:09:37,911 --> 00:09:40,705
AND I ONLY WISH
THAT I HAD SOMEONE THERE

241
00:09:40,747 --> 00:09:44,000
WHO HAD GIVEN UP BABIES
THAT COULD HAVE TOLD ME

242
00:09:44,042 --> 00:09:46,669
HOW TERRIBLE IT IS
TO GIVE UP BABIES.

243
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:47,754
( sighing softly )

244
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:48,838
I JUST THINK

245
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:50,340
THAT IT WOULD BE SOMETHING

246
00:09:50,382 --> 00:09:53,093
THAT YOU WOULD REGRET
EVERY SINGLE DAY FOR THE REST

247
00:09:53,134 --> 00:09:54,094
OF YOUR LIFE.

248
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:55,470
SO, HOWEVER HARD IT IS

249
00:09:55,512 --> 00:09:58,139
FOR YOU TO GIVE UP
THIS PUPPY, OH...

250
00:09:58,181 --> 00:10:01,976
WOULD BE, LIKE, A MILLION TIMES
HARDER TO GIVE UP A CHILD.

251
00:10:05,397 --> 00:10:08,066
I REALLY SHOULDN'T
HAVE GIVEN YOU
THE PUPPY FIRST.

252
00:10:08,108 --> 00:10:09,901
ALL RIGHT. IT'S OKAY.

253
00:10:09,943 --> 00:10:11,736
( sighs )

254
00:10:11,778 --> 00:10:13,821
OH, UH, WOULD YOU
MIND SITTING THERE?

255
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:15,115
I-I'M SAVING THIS SEAT

256
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:17,158
FOR MY FRIEND, ROSS.

257
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,785
YOU MEAN, DR. GELLER?

258
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:22,163
"DOCTOR"? OH, I DIDN'T KNOW
HE HAD A NICKNAME.

259
00:10:22,205 --> 00:10:25,292
OH, HE WON'T SIT HERE.

260
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:27,877
ONLY THE PEOPLE
IN THE WHITE COATS
SIT OVER THERE

261
00:10:27,919 --> 00:10:30,755
AND ONLY THE PEOPLE
IN THE BLUE BLAZERS
SIT OVER HERE.

262
00:10:30,797 --> 00:10:32,924
WELL, UH, H-HOW COME?

263
00:10:32,966 --> 00:10:34,134
THAT'S THE WAY IT IS.

264
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:36,303
THAT'S CRAZY.

265
00:10:36,344 --> 00:10:38,763
MAYBE IT'S CRAZY
IN A PERFECT WORLD--

266
00:10:38,805 --> 00:10:41,391
A WORLD WITHOUT LAB COATS
AND BLAZERS--

267
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:43,435
BUT YOU NOT
IN A PERFECT WORLD.

268
00:10:43,477 --> 00:10:45,270
YOU IN A MUSEUM NOW.

269
00:10:46,813 --> 00:10:49,023
SEE THAT SCIENTIST
WITH THE GLASSES?

270
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:51,359
HE AND I USED TO PLAY
TOGETHER ALL THE TIME

271
00:10:51,401 --> 00:10:52,360
IN GRADE SCHOOL.

272
00:10:52,402 --> 00:10:54,154
HMM, BUT NOW...

273
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:56,030
PETER!

274
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,698
HEY, PETER!

275
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:00,201
IT'S ME, RHONDA

276
00:11:00,243 --> 00:11:01,911
FROM P.S. 129!

277
00:11:01,953 --> 00:11:05,415
I SHARED MY PUDDING
WITH YOU, MAN.

278
00:11:06,625 --> 00:11:09,628
I GAVE YOU MY SNACK PACK!

279
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:14,799
SEE? HE PRETEND
HE DON'T EVEN HEAR ME!

280
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:17,135
I-I THINK
EVERYBODY'S
PRETENDING

281
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:18,886
THEY DON'T HEAR YOU.

282
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:20,888
LOOK, I...

283
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:22,974
I DON'T KNOW ABOUT
YOU AND YOUR JACKETS

284
00:11:23,016 --> 00:11:24,309
AND YOUR SEPARATE TABLES

285
00:11:24,351 --> 00:11:26,060
BUT ROSS IS ONE
OF MY BEST FRIENDS

286
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:27,395
AND IF I SAVE HIM A SEAT

287
00:11:27,437 --> 00:11:29,272
I'M TELLING YOU,
HE WILL SIT IN IT.

288
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:33,485
ROSS, ROSS,
OVER HERE, MAN.

289
00:11:33,527 --> 00:11:34,777
I SAVED YOU A SEAT.

290
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:38,072
THAT'S OKAY.

291
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:39,407
I'M COOL OVER HERE.

292
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:42,118
I'LL CATCH UP WITH
YOU LATER, JOEY.

293
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:47,999
OOP, THIS IS SAVED.

294
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:51,919
GIFT SHOP.

295
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:59,344
HEY, UH...

296
00:11:59,386 --> 00:12:00,719
I'M REALLY, REALLY SORRY

297
00:12:00,761 --> 00:12:03,181
ABOUT WHAT HAPPENED
IN THE CAFETERIA TODAY.

298
00:12:03,223 --> 00:12:04,599
IT'S NO BIG DEAL, YOU KNOW.

299
00:12:04,641 --> 00:12:06,518
YOU-YOU DO
WHAT YOU GOT TO DO, RIGHT?

300
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:07,810
IT'S NOT JUST ME.

301
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:10,063
I MEAN, THE SCIENTISTS
AND THE TOUR GUIDES

302
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:11,314
NEVER SIT TOGETHER.

303
00:12:12,982 --> 00:12:14,025
WHATEVER.

304
00:12:14,067 --> 00:12:15,569
IT'S LIKE THAT
EVERYWHERE, JOEY.

305
00:12:15,610 --> 00:12:17,070
OKAY, MON, BACK ME UP HERE.

306
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:18,572
WHERE YOU WORK

307
00:12:18,613 --> 00:12:20,990
THE, UH, THE WAITERS EAT
WITH THE WAITERS, RIGHT

308
00:12:21,032 --> 00:12:23,410
AND THE CHEFS EAT
WITH THE OTHER CHEFS, RIGHT?

309
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:25,412
UH, I EAT BY MYSELF
IN THE ALLEY

310
00:12:25,453 --> 00:12:27,247
BECAUSE EVERYBODY HATES ME.

311
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:32,669
LOOK, ROSS...

312
00:12:32,711 --> 00:12:34,003
REALLY, IT'S-IT'S
NO BIG DEAL.

313
00:12:34,045 --> 00:12:35,171
YOU KNOW,
YOU WEAR A WHITE COAT.

314
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:36,631
I WEAR A BLUE BLAZER.

315
00:12:36,673 --> 00:12:38,508
IF THAT MEANS WE CAN'T
BE FRIENDS AT WORK

316
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:39,842
THEN SO BE IT, YOU KNOW.

317
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:42,136
HEY, I UNDERSTAND,
YOU KNOW?

318
00:12:42,178 --> 00:12:42,970
WHEN I'M IN A PLAY

319
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:43,762
AND YOU'RE
IN THE AUDIENCE

320
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:45,223
I DON'T TALK TO YOU, RIGHT?

321
00:12:47,517 --> 00:12:50,478
SO, IT'S... YOU KNOW,
IT'S, UH, IT'S-IT'S COOL.

322
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:51,979
I'LL SEE YOU TOMORROW.

323
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:53,898
( door opening and closing )

324
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:55,900
YEAH. WHEN WE'RE
IN THE AUDIENCE

325
00:12:55,942 --> 00:12:58,111
HE DOESN'T TALK TO US,
BUT HE DOES WAVE.

326
00:13:03,116 --> 00:13:05,619
( Phoebe humming
"Rock a Bye Baby" )

327
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:07,078
( door opening )

328
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,664
HI.

329
00:13:09,706 --> 00:13:11,666
( continues humming )

330
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:13,918
WHY'S PHOEBE SINGING
TO KARL MALDEN?

331
00:13:15,128 --> 00:13:16,421
OOH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

332
00:13:16,463 --> 00:13:17,589
I THINK IT'S TIME

333
00:13:17,631 --> 00:13:19,006
FOR PUPPY
TO GO OUT AGAIN.

334
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:20,799
COME ON. LET'S GO
TO THE BALCONY.

335
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:21,800
WHAT?

336
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:23,010
UH... THE STREET.

337
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:24,471
COME ON.
LET'S GO TO THE STREET.

338
00:13:24,512 --> 00:13:26,681
OH, LISTEN,
DON'T GO ON THE BALCONY

339
00:13:26,723 --> 00:13:28,224
UNTIL AFTER I GET BACK.

340
00:13:29,768 --> 00:13:30,727
( door closing )

341
00:13:30,769 --> 00:13:32,145
SO... DID YOU DO IT?

342
00:13:32,186 --> 00:13:34,897
YES, YES, WE HAD THE SEX.

343
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:37,108
UH-OH. IT WAS BAD?

344
00:13:37,150 --> 00:13:40,069
IT WAS FINE, YOU KNOW,
BUT SHE DIDN'T AGREE WITH ME

345
00:13:40,111 --> 00:13:42,196
AS STRONGLY
AS SHE AGREED WITH JOEY.

346
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:44,324
SHE WAS MORE, LIKE, UH

347
00:13:44,365 --> 00:13:45,784
"OH, I SEE YOUR POINT.

348
00:13:45,824 --> 00:13:47,744
( noncommittal: )
I'M ALL RIGHT WITH IT."

349
00:13:47,786 --> 00:13:49,788
WELL, I MEAN,
IT WAS THE FIRST TIME.

350
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:51,414
YOU KNOW,
THERE'S NOT ALWAYS

351
00:13:51,456 --> 00:13:53,374
A LOT OF AGREEMENT
THE FIRST TIME.

352
00:13:53,416 --> 00:13:55,710
YEAH. NOT FOR
GIRLS ANYWAY.

353
00:13:55,752 --> 00:13:57,796
GUYS AGREE...
LIKE THAT.

354
00:13:57,836 --> 00:13:59,964
LOOK, YOU HAVE
TO HELP ME, OKAY?

355
00:14:00,006 --> 00:14:02,634
I MEAN, I KNOW WHAT
TO DO WITH A WOMAN.

356
00:14:02,676 --> 00:14:05,345
YOU KNOW, I KNOW
WHERE EVERYTHING GOES.

357
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:08,055
IT'S ALWAYS... NICE,
BUT I NEED TO KNOW

358
00:14:08,097 --> 00:14:09,808
WHAT MAKES IT GO FROM NICE

359
00:14:09,848 --> 00:14:12,310
TO "MY GOD, SOMEBODY'S
KILLING HER IN THERE."

360
00:14:12,352 --> 00:14:14,479
ALL RIGHT. I'M GOING
TO SHOW YOU SOMETHING

361
00:14:14,521 --> 00:14:15,814
A LOT OF GUYS DON'T KNOW.

362
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:17,524
RACH, HAND ME
THAT PAD, PLEASE.

363
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:20,443
ALL RIGHT.

364
00:14:20,485 --> 00:14:21,778
NOW...

365
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:23,488
WELL, YOU DON'T
HAVE TO DRAW

366
00:14:23,530 --> 00:14:26,658
AN ACTUAL WO...
WHOA, SHE'S HOT.

367
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:29,828
NOW, EVERYBODY KNOWS
THE BASIC EROGENOUS ZONES.

368
00:14:29,868 --> 00:14:31,663
YOU GOT ONE, TWO, THREE...

369
00:14:31,705 --> 00:14:32,872
FOUR...

370
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:34,165
FIVE...

371
00:14:34,207 --> 00:14:37,084
SIX AND SEVEN.

372
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:39,504
THERE ARE SEVEN?

373
00:14:39,546 --> 00:14:42,131
LET ME SEE THAT.

374
00:14:42,173 --> 00:14:43,675
OH, YEAH.

375
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:46,386
THAT'S ONE?

376
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:47,387
( chuckling )

377
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:48,847
KIND OF AN IMPORTANT ONE.

378
00:14:48,887 --> 00:14:50,306
OH, YOU KNOW...

379
00:14:50,348 --> 00:14:52,559
YOU KNOW WHAT?
I WAS LOOKING AT
IT UPSIDE DOWN.

380
00:14:54,352 --> 00:14:55,520
( laughs )

381
00:14:55,562 --> 00:14:58,064
WELL, YOU KNOW,
SOMETIMES THAT HELPS.

382
00:15:02,943 --> 00:15:05,822
OKAY. NOW, MOST GUYS WILL HIT,
UH, ONE, TWO, THREE

383
00:15:05,864 --> 00:15:07,990
AND THEN GO TO SEVEN
AND SET UP CAMP.

384
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:11,369
TH-THAT'S BAD?

385
00:15:11,411 --> 00:15:12,829
WELL, IF YOU GO TO DISNEYLAND

386
00:15:12,871 --> 00:15:15,540
YOU DON'T SPEND THE WHOLE DAY
ON THE MATTERHORN.

387
00:15:15,582 --> 00:15:18,251
WELL, YOU MIGHT, IF IT
WERE ANYTHING LIKE SEVEN.

388
00:15:19,419 --> 00:15:20,420
Monica:
ALL RIGHT.

389
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:22,255
UH, THE IMPORTANT THING

390
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:23,548
IS TO TAKE YOUR TIME.

391
00:15:23,590 --> 00:15:25,299
YOU WANT TO HIT THEM ALL

392
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:26,885
AND YOU WANT TO MIX THEM UP.

393
00:15:26,925 --> 00:15:28,803
YOU GOT TO KEEP THEM
ON THEIR TOES.

394
00:15:28,845 --> 00:15:30,096
OH, TOES!

395
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:36,436
YEAH...

396
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:38,229
FOR SOME PEOPLE.

397
00:15:38,271 --> 00:15:39,898
Monica:
ALL RIGHT.

398
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,190
YOU COULD, UH

399
00:15:41,232 --> 00:15:43,902
START OUT WITH
A-A LITTLE ONE...

400
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:45,069
A TWO...

401
00:15:45,111 --> 00:15:47,071
A ONE, TWO, THREE...

402
00:15:47,113 --> 00:15:48,948
A THREE...

403
00:15:50,116 --> 00:15:51,492
A FIVE...

404
00:15:51,534 --> 00:15:53,494
A FOUR...

405
00:15:53,536 --> 00:15:55,162
A THREE, TWO...

406
00:15:55,204 --> 00:15:56,247
TWO...

407
00:15:56,289 --> 00:15:57,582
A TWO, FOUR, SIX...

408
00:15:57,624 --> 00:15:59,292
TWO, FOUR, SIX...

409
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:00,293
FOUR...

410
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:02,211
TWO...

411
00:16:02,253 --> 00:16:03,922
TWO...

412
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:05,047
FOUR, SEVEN...

413
00:16:06,132 --> 00:16:07,467
FIVE, SEVEN...

414
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:08,802
SIX, SEVEN...

415
00:16:08,843 --> 00:16:09,803
SEVEN...

416
00:16:09,844 --> 00:16:10,804
SEVEN...

417
00:16:10,845 --> 00:16:13,473
SEVEN, SEVEN,
SEVEN...

418
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:15,099
SEVEN, SEVEN, SEVEN...

419
00:16:15,141 --> 00:16:16,309
SEVEN!

420
00:16:17,477 --> 00:16:18,728
( silently: )
SEVEN.

421
00:16:30,657 --> 00:16:31,574
DR. GELLER...

422
00:16:31,616 --> 00:16:33,200
THERE'S A SEAT OVER HERE.

423
00:16:33,242 --> 00:16:35,829
THANK YOU, DR. PHILLIPS...

424
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:38,164
BUT I'M HAVING MY LUNCH

425
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:41,918
AT THIS TABLE,
HERE IN THE MIDDLE.

426
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,795
I'M HAVING MY LUNCH

427
00:16:43,837 --> 00:16:47,757
RIGHT HERE
WITH MY GOOD FRIEND JOEY...

428
00:16:47,799 --> 00:16:50,050
IF HE'LL SIT WITH ME.

429
00:16:55,556 --> 00:16:57,642
I WILL SIT WITH YOU,
DR. GELLER.

430
00:17:02,647 --> 00:17:07,694
YOU KNOW, WE WORK
IN A MUSEUM OF NATURAL HISTORY

431
00:17:07,735 --> 00:17:12,114
AND YET, THERE IS SOMETHING...
UNNATURAL

432
00:17:12,156 --> 00:17:15,117
ABOUT THE WAY WE EAT LUNCH.

433
00:17:15,159 --> 00:17:16,703
NOW...

434
00:17:16,744 --> 00:17:19,747
I LOOK AROUND THIS CAFETERIA
AND YOU KNOW WHAT I SEE?

435
00:17:19,789 --> 00:17:21,123
I SEE-I SEE DIVISION--

436
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:24,084
DIVISION BETWEEN PEOPLE
IN WHITE COATS

437
00:17:24,126 --> 00:17:26,170
AND PEOPLE IN BLUE BLAZERS

438
00:17:26,212 --> 00:17:28,798
AND I ASK MYSELF,
"MY GOD, WHY?!"

439
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:34,345
NOW, I SAY WE SHED
THESE-THESE COATS

440
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:36,014
THAT SEPARATE US

441
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:40,226
AND WE GET
TO KNOW THE PEOPLE UNDERNEATH.

442
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:44,480
I'M ROSS.

443
00:17:44,522 --> 00:17:47,066
I'M DIVORCED
AND I HAVE A KID.

444
00:17:54,072 --> 00:17:55,199
I'M JOEY.

445
00:17:55,241 --> 00:17:56,826
I'M AN ACTOR.

446
00:17:56,868 --> 00:18:01,163
I DON'T KNOW SQUAT
ABOUT DINOSAURS.

447
00:18:02,415 --> 00:18:05,501
I'M TED AND I JUST
MOVED HERE A MONTH AGO

448
00:18:05,543 --> 00:18:07,754
AND NEW YORK
REALLY SCARES ME.

449
00:18:07,795 --> 00:18:09,129
ALL RIGHT.
THERE YOU GO!

450
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:10,965
YEAH. YOU HANG
IN THERE, TEDDY.

451
00:18:12,008 --> 00:18:13,384
I'M ANDREW...

452
00:18:13,426 --> 00:18:16,679
AND I DIDN'T PAY
FOR THIS PEAR.

453
00:18:17,764 --> 00:18:20,600
OKAY. GOOD-GOOD FOR YOU.

454
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:22,435
I'M RHONDA...

455
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:25,605
AND THESE AREN'T REAL!

456
00:18:29,776 --> 00:18:30,902
WOW, RHONDA.

457
00:18:30,944 --> 00:18:32,070
UH...

458
00:18:33,571 --> 00:18:34,488
I'M SCOTT...

459
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,532
YEAH. OKAY, SCOTT!

460
00:18:36,574 --> 00:18:38,534
AND I NEED
TO FLIP THE LIGHT SWITCH

461
00:18:38,576 --> 00:18:40,912
ON AND OFF 17 TIMES
BEFORE I LEAVE A ROOM

462
00:18:40,954 --> 00:18:42,288
OR MY FAMILY WILL DIE.

463
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:49,629
MY MOM'S GOING TO
BE HERE ANY MINUTE.

464
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:50,713
I CAN'T DO THIS.

465
00:18:50,755 --> 00:18:51,923
I CAN'T GIVE HIM UP.

466
00:18:51,965 --> 00:18:53,049
( sighs )

467
00:18:53,091 --> 00:18:54,634
YES. NO, I CAN.

468
00:18:54,675 --> 00:18:56,594
I DON'T WANT TO...

469
00:18:56,636 --> 00:18:58,096
BUT I CAN.

470
00:18:59,263 --> 00:19:01,099
NO.

471
00:19:01,139 --> 00:19:02,767
OH, I CAN'T WATCH THIS.

472
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:04,769
IT'S LIKE SOPHIE'S CHOICE.

473
00:19:05,937 --> 00:19:08,106
YOU KNOW, I
NEVER SAW THAT.

474
00:19:08,188 --> 00:19:09,899
OH, IT WAS ONLY OKAY.

475
00:19:09,941 --> 00:19:11,525
( Phoebe groaning )

476
00:19:11,567 --> 00:19:12,735
I CAN'T DO THIS.

477
00:19:12,777 --> 00:19:14,112
MY MOM WAS RIGHT.

478
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:16,614
IF I CAN'T,
IF I CAN'T GIVE HIM UP

479
00:19:16,656 --> 00:19:20,409
THEN... THERE'S NO WAY
I CAN GIVE UP A LITTLE BABY.

480
00:19:20,451 --> 00:19:24,622
OH, GOD, FRANK AND ALICE
ARE GOING TO BE SO CRUSHED.

481
00:19:24,664 --> 00:19:26,916
WH-WHAT ELSE,
WHAT ELSE CAN I GIVE THEM?

482
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:28,501
A KIDNEY.

483
00:19:30,086 --> 00:19:31,045
HI.

484
00:19:31,087 --> 00:19:32,379
All:
HI.

485
00:19:32,421 --> 00:19:34,590
UM, WE WERE JUST IN
THE NEIGHBORHOOD, SO...

486
00:19:34,632 --> 00:19:36,175
SO WE JUST THOUGHT
WE'D STOP BY

487
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:38,469
AND LET YOU KNOW
THERE'S STILL NO PRESSURE.

488
00:19:38,511 --> 00:19:40,138
Alice:
NONE, BUT
IF THERE WAS

489
00:19:40,178 --> 00:19:41,806
SOMETHING YOU
WANTED TO TELL US

490
00:19:41,848 --> 00:19:44,809
WE'RE JUST GOING
TO BE RIGHT OVER
THERE HAVING COFFEE.

491
00:19:44,851 --> 00:19:46,894
OKAY.

492
00:19:46,936 --> 00:19:48,646
OH, WHO'S THIS LITTLE GUY?

493
00:19:48,688 --> 00:19:50,481
OH. OH!

494
00:19:50,523 --> 00:19:51,816
UM...

495
00:19:51,858 --> 00:19:52,984
OH, HE'S SO CUTE.

496
00:19:53,026 --> 00:19:55,111
HE REMINDS ME
OF MY OLD DOG, TUMOR.

497
00:19:55,153 --> 00:19:56,112
OH, OH.

498
00:19:56,154 --> 00:19:58,447
( Frank laughing )

499
00:19:58,489 --> 00:20:01,575
YOU ARE SO PRECIOUS. I
COULD JUST TAKE YOU HOME.

500
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:02,618
( Frank laughing )

501
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:04,120
HEY, WHY DON'T YOU?

502
00:20:04,162 --> 00:20:05,830
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

503
00:20:05,872 --> 00:20:07,165
UH-HUH. YEAH.

504
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:08,166
OH...

505
00:20:08,206 --> 00:20:09,750
OH, THANKS.

506
00:20:09,792 --> 00:20:11,752
( laughing )

507
00:20:11,794 --> 00:20:13,171
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

508
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:15,339
NO. I'M REALLY
OKAY WITH THIS.

509
00:20:15,381 --> 00:20:16,340
YOU KNOW WHY?

510
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:17,967
'CAUSE LOOK AT THEM.

511
00:20:18,009 --> 00:20:20,011
LOOK HOW HAPPY
THEY ARE...

512
00:20:20,053 --> 00:20:24,015
AND I MADE THAT, SO, YOU KNOW...
I KNOW IT'S GOING TO BE, LIKE

513
00:20:24,057 --> 00:20:26,893
A MILLION TIMES HARDER
TO GIVE UP A BABY

514
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:28,561
BUT, OH, MY GOD

515
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:32,565
IT'S GOING TO FEEL, LIKE,
A MILLION TIMES BETTER, RIGHT?

516
00:20:34,025 --> 00:20:35,317
I'M WANT TO DO THIS.

517
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:37,070
I WANT TO CARRY YOUR BABY.

518
00:20:37,111 --> 00:20:38,445
OH...

519
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:39,822
OH...

520
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:41,199
OH...

521
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:43,701
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

522
00:20:43,743 --> 00:20:46,412
YOU DON'T KNOW WHAT
THIS MEANS TO US.

523
00:20:46,453 --> 00:20:47,914
OH...

524
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:50,583
OH, MY GOD,
I THINK I'M GOING TO CRY.

525
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:53,044
OH, MY GOD.

526
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:57,255
IT'S GOING
TO BE SO GREAT.

527
00:20:57,297 --> 00:20:58,340
UH-HUH.

528
00:20:58,382 --> 00:21:00,176
HI.

529
00:21:00,218 --> 00:21:01,510
WHAT'S GOING ON?

530
00:21:01,552 --> 00:21:03,721
OH! I-I GAVE THEM
THE PUPPY

531
00:21:03,763 --> 00:21:06,933
AND IT MADE THEM SO HAPPY
THAT I DECIDED I'M GOING

532
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:08,059
TO CARRY THEIR BABY.

533
00:21:08,101 --> 00:21:09,060
UH, PHOEBE...

534
00:21:09,102 --> 00:21:10,603
NO, NO, I KNOW.

535
00:21:10,644 --> 00:21:12,813
YOU AND I ARE TOTALLY
DIFFERENT PEOPLE, THOUGH

536
00:21:12,855 --> 00:21:14,941
AND THIS IS
A TOTALLY DIFFERENT SITUATION

537
00:21:14,982 --> 00:21:17,401
AND I KNOW THAT
I AM NOT GOING TO REGRET THIS.

538
00:21:17,443 --> 00:21:20,196
OH, I-I UNDERSTAND ALL THAT.

539
00:21:20,238 --> 00:21:23,157
IT'S JUST...
THAT WAS MY PUPPY.

540
00:21:23,199 --> 00:21:24,450
OH...

541
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:31,165
WOULD YOU SURROGATE?

542
00:21:31,207 --> 00:21:32,833
IT DEPENDS WHO ASKED.

543
00:21:32,875 --> 00:21:34,794
WHAT IF I ASKED?

544
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:36,503
OH, MON...

545
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:37,630
SURE.

546
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:38,631
REALLY?

547
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:40,007
YES.

548
00:21:42,468 --> 00:21:45,012
YOU'RE NOT ASKING ME, ARE YOU?

549
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:46,264
NO.

550
00:21:46,304 --> 00:21:48,348
YES, TOTALLY.

551
00:21:50,143 --> 00:21:52,103
( gasps )

552
00:21:52,145 --> 00:21:53,646
THANK YOU.

553
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:55,231
THANK YOU.

554
00:21:55,273 --> 00:21:56,690
THANK YOU.

555
00:21:56,732 --> 00:21:58,859
YES! THANK YOU!

556
00:21:58,901 --> 00:22:01,695
